-- title:
--   Frobenius trace a_ℓ(g) on a newform eigenplane
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense, i.e. a normalised eigenform for which `GoodEigensystemOccursAt g M'` fails for every proper divisor $M'$ of $M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals, and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)$ equal to the $\ell$-th coefficient of the level-one $q$-expansion of $g$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$. Let $O''$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a characteristic-zero field which is an $O''$-algebra, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $K$. Give $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the Hecke-module structure `heckeModuleBar M`, and let $T=$ [`TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the module of sequences $x$ in $J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\, x_{n+1}=x_n$. Assume given: a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ whose scalar action is computed level by level, $(a\cdot x)_n=(a \bmod \lambda^n)\,x_n$; a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ with $\rho_M(\sigma)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes y$ whenever the sequence of $y$ is $\sigma$ applied to that of $x$; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from `HeckeAlg` $=\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \mathrm{Nat.Primes}\ \mathbb Z$ to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes T)$ with $T_M(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$; and a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ of $K$-dimension $2$, stable under the base change of every $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which the base change of $T_M(\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\ell)$ acts by the scalar $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$. The conclusion: for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$ and $\ell\ne\lambda$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ and inducing $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the $K$-trace of the restriction of $(\rho_M\sigma)\otimes K$ to $W$ equals $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))$, that is, $\varphi(a_\ell(g))$.
--
--   This is the trace half of the Eichler–Shimura description of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two newform: on the $\varphi\circ\chi_g$-eigenplane inside the $\lambda$-adic Tate module of $J_0(M)$, an arithmetic Frobenius at a prime $\ell\nmid M\lambda$ outside $S$ has trace $a_\ell(g)$. It is used to produce the pinned eigenplane of the newform and, from there, the $\lambda$-adic Galois representation with its prescribed local behaviour.
